  "findings": [
    "Initial concurrent clones produced stale working copies and no first daemon acknowledgement. Preserved the sole payload outside the workspace, explicitly updated each stale workspace, then restored it and verified publication. This is an operator workaround, not a fixed clone issue.",
    "Initial foreground serve omitted an explicit control socket, so default server status reported running=false despite healthy authenticated HTTP. Recovery launches use an explicit socket.",
    "Timing controller physical location is unverified; FI/HEL records network egress only. The three provider-verified VMs are all Dallas, not separate geographical regions.",
    "heads-before capture exited 1 because the status control socket was absent. Its heads GET succeeded; heads-stable and subsequent explicit-socket warm/cold/post-cold status checks passed. Not every attempted command passed.",
    "publish-a-ack initially timed out with no acknowledgement, but its shell wrapper returned the following cat exit code (0). Treat that attempt as failed, not successful. publish-a-aligned used set -e and required an actual acknowledgement."
  ],
